    "description": "OPB is an agency directly under the Governor to assist in policymaking determining short and long-range plans for Georgia as a basis for budget recommendations to the Legislature.\n\nCreated and maintained several Statewide Enterprise Web Based Applications revolving around state budget processing, capital outlay budgeting, and issues tracking systems using ASP, ASP.Net, C#, VBScript, Jscript, HTML, CSS for the front end, and SQL Server 2005 for the back end.\n\nTrained employees on new Statewide Enterprise Web Based Applications.\n\nIn the process of converting several classic ASP websites to ASP.net and Active Reports .Net\n\nDeveloped a metadata .Net Win Forms application which connects directly to SQL 2005 database server.\n\nWrote several off-line applications for data export for reporting purposes.\n\nWrote and maintained over 400 reports using active reports and VB Com objects which feed data from agencies input into the budget processing websites.\n\nWrote queries and stored procedures on the fly to retrieve data requested by the governors’ analysis.\n\nLead feasibility studies regarding user requests.\n\nUsed Team Foundation Server and Visual SourceSafe for version control for all reports, web and desktop applications.",
